config REALTEK_DISPLAY_ENABLE_VCDJ
    bool "Enable VeriSilicon VC9000DJ DecoderJ (JPEG/PNG hardware decode)"
    depends on REALTEK_DISPLAY
    default n
    help
        Driver for the VeriSilicon (Hantro) VC9000DJ DecoderJ image decoding IP,
        hardware build ID 0x2070. JPEG and PNG are the two formats this IP
        decodes and both are always compiled in. This is a different IP from the
        Realtek JPU selected by REALTEK_DISPLAY_ENABLE_JPU; the two can be
        enabled independently and share no register or clock code.

        The register base, IRQ, clock and reset contract for this SoC has not
        been delivered yet, so the low level layer is still placeholder code.
        Enabling this option gives a driver that compiles, links and can walk the
        whole vendor Control Software call path, not one that decodes pictures.

if REALTEK_DISPLAY_ENABLE_VCDJ

choice REALTEK_VCDJ_COMPLETION
    prompt "VCDJ hardware completion detection"
    default REALTEK_VCDJ_POLLING
    help
        How the driver waits for the decoder core to finish a job.

config REALTEK_VCDJ_POLLING
    bool "Polling (bring-up default)"
    help
        Poll the decoder interrupt status register with a wall clock bounded
        timeout. Requires no IRQ information, which is why it is the bring-up
        default.

config REALTEK_VCDJ_IRQ
    bool "Interrupt"
    help
        Wait on a semaphore released by the decoder interrupt handler. Needs the
        IRQ number and routing, which are not known yet, so the platform layer
        currently refuses this mode and the core layer falls back to polling.

endchoice

config REALTEK_VCDJ_HW_TIMEOUT_MS
    int "Upper bound for any hardware wait (ms)"
    default 2000
    range 1 60000
    help
        Hard ceiling applied to every DWLWaitHwReady() call. The vendor call
        sites pass DEC_X170_TIMEOUT_LENGTH, which defaults to -1 meaning "wait
        forever"; that value is clamped to this bound so a missing or wedged core
        can never hang the caller.

config REALTEK_VCDJ_COND_WAIT_TIMEOUT_MS
    int "Upper bound for condition variable and semaphore waits (ms)"
    default 1000
    range 1 60000
    help
        With NON_PTHREAD_H the vendor code turns pthread_create() into a no-op,
        so nothing exists to signal a condition variable. Every vendor call site
        re-checks its predicate in a loop, so bounding the wait turns a potential
        deadlock into a slow poll.

config REALTEK_VCDJ_OS_MUTEX_COUNT
    int "Number of OS mutex objects reserved for the vendor code"
    default 12
    range 1 32
    help
        The vendor code creates its mutexes through the dwl_os bridge, which hands
        out indices into a statically sized pool. Exhaustion is reported as a hard
        error rather than silently ignored. The upper bound of 32 comes from the
        allocation bitmap being a single 32-bit word.

config REALTEK_VCDJ_OS_COND_COUNT
    int "Number of OS condition variable objects reserved for the vendor code"
    default 8
    range 1 32
    help
        See REALTEK_VCDJ_OS_MUTEX_COUNT. OSIF has no condition variable, so each
        one is emulated with a binary semaphore.

config REALTEK_VCDJ_OS_SEM_COUNT
    int "Number of OS semaphore objects reserved for the vendor code"
    default 12
    range 1 32
    help
        See REALTEK_VCDJ_OS_MUTEX_COUNT.

config REALTEK_VCDJ_SELFTEST
    bool "Build the VCDJ bring-up self test"
    default n
    help
        Compiles hal_vcdj_selftest(), which walks the whole vendor call path
        (DWLInit -> JpegDecInit -> JpegDecGetImageInfo -> JpegDecSetInfo ->
        JpegDecDecode -> bounded hardware wait) and reports every step over the
        console with printf().

        It also cross-checks the vendor software header parse against an
        independent scan of the same bitstream, which is the only real functional
        verification possible before the hardware contract arrives.

        Leave this off in a production image: it pulls in printf() and the
        diagnostics are only useful during bring-up.

endif # REALTEK_DISPLAY_ENABLE_VCDJ

